VU1 timing (patch 82): name the block/chain sampling strides, document the block-entry timing invariants

The 1/8 block and 1/16 chain rdtsc samples were literals (& 7u / & 15u) at the two call sites; the stride is part of
what a counter means (the reported ticks are scaled by it), so it is now kBlockSampleStride/kChainSampleStride and
used at both sites. The block-entry timing predicate (idle table only when nothing read is in flight, memo only
against the same predecessor identity, chain path in lockstep with the memo) was only implied by the code; it is
now stated next to blockTiming, together with the relative/absolute cycle convention and the entry-flag ordering.

No behaviour change: same strides, same predicate, same table.

