+// Invariants of VU block entry timing:
+//  - The returned table holds the issue cycles of the block's pairs *relative* to vu.m_cycle at entry; the absolute
+//    cycle of pair i is vu.m_cycle + cyc[i]. Only the block's reads of lanes written by a pair still in flight from the
+//    previous block can push a cycle past the idle table; everything else uses the idle table.
+//  - The idle table is exact only when no such read is in flight (and the flag queue is empty); otherwise the exact
+//    engine's stall model is run for the distinct (lane, slack) set and cached.
+//  - The memo may answer only when the predecessor ended exactly at `start`, its span is >= maxLat (so no lane can
+//    still be in flight), every array is ready, and the predecessor's timing identity (bt/cycId) is unchanged. The
+//    chain path (vu1nMemoTry) tests the exact same predicate; if the two ever disagreed, a block would be timed against
+//    the wrong predecessor, so keep them in lockstep (patch 76).
+//  - Entry flags are imported outside this function (syncInflight); blockTiming never mutates state, it only chooses
+//    the timing table.
 // Issue cycles (relative to vu.m_cycle) of the block's pairs: the idle table unless a lane it reads is still in flight
 // past that read; then the exact engine's stall model, run once per distinct (lane, slack) set and cached.
